## Session 2 — Moving to Private Repo

### Context
- User is on **Windows** and wants to move this project to a private GitHub repo
- Installed GitHub CLI on Windows via `winget install GitHub.cli`
- Authenticated with `gh auth login` on their Windows machine

### Git remotes (in sandbox)
- `origin` → `pganzy-commits/everything-claude-code` (public, via local proxy)
- `private` → `https://github.com/pganzy-commits/my-claude-code-setup.git` (added but can't auth from sandbox)

### What's left to do (on user's Windows machine)
1. Create the private repo if it doesn't exist:
   ```powershell
   gh repo create my-claude-code-setup --private
   ```
2. Push everything to the private repo:
   ```powershell
   cd ~\everything-claude-code
   git remote add private https://github.com/pganzy-commits/my-claude-code-setup.git
   git push private --all
   git push private --tags
   ```
3. Remove the branch from the public origin:
   ```powershell
   git push origin --delete claude/new-project-setup-SJjFj
   ```

### Status
- Sandbox environment cannot authenticate to the private repo
- User needs to complete the push from their local Windows machine
